{
  "_what_this_is": "Keyword list for the advisory personal-data pre-screen (pipeline/prescreen.py). GDPR Art. 9 special categories, Art. 10 criminal-offence data, and data about children, in Greek and English. A hit means 'a person should look at this line', never 'this is special-category data'; a miss proves nothing.",
  "_status": "Advisory only. Never blocking, never a control: the human screening step in docs/pilot/DATA_PROTECTION.md section 10 remains the control. Proposed synthetic default; the data-protection lead reviews and extends it before pilot use (OWNER/DPO TO CONFIRM).",
  "_matching": "Text and terms are both normalised: Unicode NFD, combining marks (Greek tonos, dialytika) removed, casefolded, final sigma folded to sigma. 'prefix' terms match at the start of a word (so 'diagnos' matches 'diagnosis' and 'diagnosed'); 'word' terms match a whole word or phrase only (for short or ambiguous stems). Spaces inside a term match any run of whitespace.",
  "_known_limits": "High recall on purpose: health-product, political-campaign or children's-product clients will produce hits on ordinary brief language. Greek 'πολιτική' (also 'policy') is deliberately NOT a term. No term list can find a special category expressed indirectly.",
